Why This Market Matters
Loitering munitions combine reconnaissance, target acquisition, and terminal strike capabilities, giving military units additional options for precision engagement. Their expanding role in defense planning is increasing attention on range, autonomy, electronic-warfare resilience, production capacity, and affordability. At the same time, counter-drone defenses, jamming, export controls, and system complexity remain important challenges for manufacturers and procurement agencies.

